      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n`LLM.reset_prefix_cache(reset_connector=True)` returns `True` even when Mooncake fails to clear the Store.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\nThe worker's RESET handler calls `store.remove_all(force=True)` and always replies ACK. The SDK reports failure by returning a negative `ErrorCode` rather than raising, so the result was dropped. The scheduler already maps a worker NACK to `False`.\r\n\r\n## Change\r\n\r\nNACK when `remove_all()` returns a negative value:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nremoved = self.store_worker.store.remove_all(force=True)\r\nif removed < 0:\r\n    logger.error(\"Mooncake remove_all failed with error code %d.\", removed)\r\n    self.socket.send(RESP_ERR)\r\n```\r\n\r\nExceptions still NACK as before; the send-queue drain is unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Relationship to other work\r\n\r\n#58670 also touches reset handling but does not check the removal result. Scoping the reset to `cache_prefix` is left to a follow-up PR.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Mooncake store unit tests and pre-commit pass. The new test fails on main for a negative result.\r\n- Native Mooncake Master (TCP), Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct: generate, then call `reset_prefix_cache(reset_connector=True)` with the Master running and again after killing it.\r\n\r\n| | Master running | Master killed |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| main | `True` | `True` |\r\n| This PR | `True` | `False` (`remove_all` returned -900) |\r\n\r\n## AI assistance\r\n\r\nClaude Code was used for implementation, tests, and drafting. The submitter reviewed the change and ran the checks above.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>",
